{"name":"Ethereal One","hex":"#dedeb6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ethereal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the presupposition of an invisible air-like element permeating all of space, or to the higher regions beyond the earth or beyond the atmosphere.","Pertaining to the immaterial realm, as symbolically represented by, or (in earlier epochs) conflated with, such atmospheric and extra-atmospheric concepts."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of ethereal wave (“music genre”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ethereal"},{"term":"one","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 1."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Oneida."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/one"}],"entries":[{"title":"1","blocks":[{"text":"1 is a number, numeral, and grapheme. It is the first and smallest positive integer of the infinite sequence of natural numbers. This fundamental property has led to its unique uses in other fields, ranging from science to sports, where it commonly denotes the first, leading, or top thing in a group. 1 is the unit of counting or measurement, and represents a single thing. The representation of 1 evolved from ancient Sumerian and Babylonian symbols to the modern Arabic numeral. Linguistically, in English, \"one\" is a determiner for singular nouns and a gender-neutral pronoun."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg/500px-Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard.jpg/1280px-Woodstock_typewriter%2C_1940s%2C_daylight_-_keyboard